TOPIC – 1: DBMS (Data base management system)

What is Data?
It is a raw fact (i.e. character, numbers, special character, and symbols)
Data will never give meaningful statements
Ex. 1001 is a data     SMITH is a data    1st- jan-2025 is a data
    1002 is a data     SHIVANI is a data 2nd- jan-2025 is a data
    1003 is a data     Cherry is a data 3rd- jan-2025 is a data

What is Information?
- Processing data is called as “information”
- Information is always providing meaningful statement 
     Employee_ID        Employee_Name      Hiredate 
 Ex.      1001 is a data     SMITH is a data     1st- jan-2025 is a data
    1002 is a data     SHIVANI is a data   2nd- jan-2025 is a data
          1003 is a data     Cherry is a data    3rd- jan-2025 is a data

What is Database?
It is a collection of information which belongs to one business organization.
It is a memory which is used to store collection of inter related data/information of an organization.
Ex: Bank_Database, University_Database, Healthcare_Database.

Ex:
Bank_Database
 
- Tbl_Bank
          -bcode , bankname , bloc
- Tbl_Dept
          - dept name, deptbranch, deptloc
- Tbl_Employee
          - empname, empid, empbranch, empdept, empsalary
- Tbl_Customer
          - A/c num, Cname, Mbno, Address
- Tbl_Accounts
          - A/c num, A/c type, balance
-Tbl_Transactions
          -A/c num, tran type, tran date, tran time, amount



TYPES OF DATABASES:
There are 2 types of databases.
1. OLTP (Online transaction processing)
2. OLAP (Online analytical processing)

